WEBVTT

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:21.620
Both today and tomorrow, I've got time to kick back.

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:21.620
kyou mo ashita mo HIMAKKUSU

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:24.830
My family of four and I are going to stay the night.

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:24.830
gokazoku yonin de goippaku

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.670
Put on an Egyptian front and become a sphinx,

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.670
EGIPUTO kidori de SUFINKUSU

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:30.420
and for an American feeling, Texas!

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:30.420
AMERICA kibun de TEXAS

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.470
When you're sitting pretty, with enough and to spare,

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.470
yoyuu SHAKUSHAKUPPE itsumo

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.680
and yet you always shilly-shally,

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.680
funya funya de iruto

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:39.930
and your bitter face and bitter feelings both teeter-totter,

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:39.930
nigamushi hara no mushi nahe nahe to

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:43.390
it's time to get out of there!

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:43.390
tettai shichau yo

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:46.690
I am feeling Ultra Relax,

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:46.690
watashi ha URUTORA RIRAKKUSU

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:49.940
a wonderful, invincible Relax.

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:49.940
SUTEKI ni muteki na RIRAKKUSU

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:52.860
A one-step-above kind of Deluxe.

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:52.860
hito aji chigau ze DERAKKUSU

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:54.070
I may be a little jumbled,

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:54.070
toccharakatte mo

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:55.820
but when I'm called on, ba-ba-ba-ba-bang!

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:55.820
yobarerya PAPAPAPAAAN!

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:58.910
I always feel Relax,

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:58.910
watashi ha itsudemo RIRAKKUSU

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.910
a humble, simple, sort of Deluxe.

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.910
WABISABI kikasete DERAKKUSU

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:04.830
Bright! Clear! Alert-headed, peep-peep!

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:04.830
BIKKARI! KIKKARI! saeteru ATAMA PII! PII!

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:07.960
Keep your eyes on me, okay?!

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:07.960
watashi no KOTO dake mitete ne!

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:35.780
I am Kurata Sana, a middle school 1st year acting talent!

00:01:35.780 --> 00:01:37.570
My manager, Rei-kun!

00:01:37.570 --> 00:01:40.240
A look-alike of my Japanese friend, Brad!

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:41.870
The mysterious white bat, Babbit!

00:01:41.870 --> 00:01:44.370
Love You, Love You, Love...

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:47.580
Broadway's choreographer Michelle Hamilton.

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:50.380
The Hamilton's only daughter, Sicil.

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:54.880
My brave-hearted but gentle ally in the New York adventures, Naozumi-kun.

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:56.420
Naozumi...

00:01:58.550 --> 00:02:01.850
Sana-chan, the lady we met yesterday was my mother.

00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:04.430
I found you!

00:02:05.220 --> 00:02:08.850
I couldn't help coming to see you!

00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:13.780
I Know Too Much!
My Secret!

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:18.070
Here you are, some milk.
Calm yourself.

00:02:18.070 --> 00:02:20.160
Thank you... umm...

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:22.740
Bernadette. Call me Bernie.

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:26.370
I am making some delicious turkey, so hang on a little.

00:02:26.370 --> 00:02:29.170
Rei! Take good care of it,
be careful not to ruin it.

00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:33.540
Ok, ok, I understand.

00:02:33.590 --> 00:02:36.880
Coming here to visit us means...

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:40.090
...that you ran away from the mansion...

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:43.260
That's right. Because if I told mama she wouldn't allow it.

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:45.470
Which in turn means...

00:02:55.690 --> 00:02:57.280
Ah! Michelle!

00:02:57.280 --> 00:03:00.240
Michelle's here!
Wait a sec! We didn't ...

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:01.030
Mama...

00:03:01.030 --> 00:03:03.240
What's up?

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:09.040
Sicil! It's Mama! I know you are in there! Come down right now!

00:03:10.210 --> 00:03:13.540
No! I'm not going home!
I want to be with Naozumi!

00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:15.000
Sicil!

00:03:17.050 --> 00:03:19.550
Sicil, don't say such foolish things, get down here quickly!

00:03:19.550 --> 00:03:26.760
No! Because mama hates me, doesn't need me, and because I won't leave Naozumi!

00:03:26.850 --> 00:03:32.650
Sicil! Come back! Sicil! Come back immediately! Sicil!

00:03:32.650 --> 00:03:36.190
Sicil, do you hear it? Mama's voice?

00:03:36.190 --> 00:03:41.570
She knows rumors about this incident could reach Broadway, but she is here after you.

00:03:41.570 --> 00:03:44.820
Don't you think she is really worried about you?

00:03:44.820 --> 00:03:49.250
That isn't so! She just wants to keep me locked up in the mansion!

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:55.250
Because it's embarrassing that I can't dance.

00:03:55.250 --> 00:03:56.460
Can't dance?

00:03:56.460 --> 00:04:00.670
Exactly. On my stage debut, when I was 7 years old...

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:06.220
I fell from the stage and hurt myself.

00:04:06.220 --> 00:04:08.930
I couldn't stand on the stage again.

00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:12.350
The dream of becoming a pro dancer disappeared there.

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:16.980
Ah. Now that you mention it I read something about that in the papers.

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:20.070
So what if you can't dance!

00:04:20.070 --> 00:04:23.070
For the Hamiltons dancing is everything!

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:30.870
Sicil. Even if you can't dance, your mama can't just leave you alone.

00:04:31.540 --> 00:04:35.370
Because she is your mother who gave birth to you.

00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:36.670
Sicil!

00:04:36.670 --> 00:04:37.960
No!

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:39.090
Sagami-san!

00:04:40.590 --> 00:04:46.180
Could you please ask if it is okay for Sicil to stay here for a while?

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:47.470
Me?

00:04:47.470 --> 00:04:49.390
That is a good idea!

00:04:49.390 --> 00:04:52.890
It would be so great
if you did that! Please...

00:04:52.890 --> 00:04:54.770
Hold on, what do you think you are doing?!

00:04:54.770 --> 00:04:57.860
Wow, it's the first time Sana-chan's sex appeal tactics worked!

00:04:57.860 --> 00:04:59.190
What is it?

00:04:59.190 --> 00:05:06.320
I wonder if it would be alright with you if you let Sicil stay here for a while.

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:10.280
Don't joke with me. I came here to take Sicil back!

00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:15.460
Sicil! If you don't come down by yourself then I will go up and get you!

00:05:20.630 --> 00:05:22.050
Gary!

00:05:22.050 --> 00:05:24.340
Calm yourself, Michelle!

00:05:24.340 --> 00:05:28.850
If you force her to come back
her heart will close up like a shell.

00:05:28.850 --> 00:05:31.350
Just let her stay here for a while.

00:05:31.350 --> 00:05:34.270
Aren't you worried about her?

00:05:34.270 --> 00:05:39.940
Michelle. Sicil is staying here. We know the location.

00:05:39.940 --> 00:05:44.860
That's right, you don't have to worry about a thing! Just leave Sicil to me!

00:05:44.860 --> 00:05:46.530
Did you hear that, Michelle?

00:05:46.530 --> 00:05:51.370
Sagami is responsible with his life if something happens to Sicil.

00:05:51.370 --> 00:05:54.250
Excuse me, I didn't say anything like that.

00:05:54.250 --> 00:05:56.830
This is all your doing.

00:05:58.170 --> 00:06:02.040
Who is more important to you,
Sicil or the other kid?

00:06:04.050 --> 00:06:05.760
Both are.

00:06:09.890 --> 00:06:11.600
Excuse me...

00:06:11.970 --> 00:06:14.270
Take care of Sicil, Sagami.

00:06:14.270 --> 00:06:16.020
That is...

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:18.190
If something happens we will kill you.

00:06:18.190 --> 00:06:19.980
Yes... Whaaaat?!

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:22.360
We are serious.

00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:24.150
Wait a moment, that is...

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:25.280
Everything turned out well!

00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:26.570
No, it didn't!

00:06:26.570 --> 00:06:30.160
Now that everything is sorted out, let's have a welcome party!

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:31.870
This is no joke!

00:06:31.870 --> 00:06:34.160
Anyway, let's all go shopping first!

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:39.080
Shopping! This is the first time I've ever gone to the supermarket!

00:06:45.670 --> 00:06:50.550
Sicil's so... cute, isn't she?

00:06:50.760 --> 00:06:55.100
Sicil! That's dangerous!
Stop please! Sicil!

00:06:55.100 --> 00:06:59.060
To be excited that much...
we should be happy for her.

00:06:59.060 --> 00:07:04.480
Even the rich have their problems, not just us ordinary people.

00:07:04.900 --> 00:07:08.070
Eh? Where did Naozumi go?

00:07:08.070 --> 00:07:11.660
Naozumi-kun!
What are you looking at?

00:07:11.660 --> 00:07:15.740
Ah, pickles! Pickles here are different from the Japanese ones, aren't they?

00:07:15.740 --> 00:07:17.290
Because they're more spicy.

00:07:17.290 --> 00:07:19.160
What's that supposed to be?

00:07:19.540 --> 00:07:23.630
I thought we should meet, and see what happens.

00:07:25.630 --> 00:07:29.010
That person calling herself my mother...

00:07:30.470 --> 00:07:34.600
I thought I may as well listen to what she has to say.

00:07:34.600 --> 00:07:36.850
She would surely like that.

00:07:38.060 --> 00:07:39.930
Hey, Naozumi, do you like this?

00:07:39.930 --> 00:07:42.060
Ah, Naozumi-kun left for a moment.

00:07:42.440 --> 00:07:45.060
But he said he will be back before dinner.

00:07:45.060 --> 00:07:47.360
Why now, all of a sudden?

00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:48.280
Don't worry.

00:07:48.280 --> 00:07:51.950
Let's make lot of delicious stuff and surprise Naozumi-kun when he gets back!

00:07:51.950 --> 00:07:56.580
Ok! I'm going to make dinner!
Whee, I'll be cooking for Naozumi!

00:07:56.580 --> 00:07:59.250
What is it, Rick?
Why did you come back?

00:07:59.250 --> 00:08:00.660
Just something I forgot.

00:08:00.660 --> 00:08:06.040
Hurry up, get out quickly! It would be disastrous if he saw us together here!

00:08:06.040 --> 00:08:08.380
Is it all right? Hurting him like that?

00:08:08.380 --> 00:08:10.840
Worrying about my son is not your problem.

00:08:10.840 --> 00:08:15.760
It's my own business. I went through a lot of trouble to set this all up!

00:08:17.350 --> 00:08:20.520
Naozumi! It's Naozumi!

00:08:20.890 --> 00:08:22.230
Now it's your turn!

00:08:22.230 --> 00:08:23.350
You're gonna kill me!

00:08:23.350 --> 00:08:25.270
It's alright, just follow the package!

00:08:31.570 --> 00:08:34.320
You finally came! Naozumi!

00:08:36.450 --> 00:08:40.160
Come inside! Are you hungry?
I made some delicious pie for you!

00:08:40.160 --> 00:08:41.500
Yuko!

00:08:42.290 --> 00:08:43.660
Here, have all you want.

00:08:43.660 --> 00:08:49.170
I was sure you would come!
I believed in you!

00:08:49.670 --> 00:08:52.170
What's wrong, Naozumi?

00:08:53.970 --> 00:09:01.390
Are you doubting me?
About being your real mother?

00:09:02.180 --> 00:09:05.390
Oh yes, wait a moment!
I will let you see the records.

00:09:05.390 --> 00:09:09.320
I will find it in a moment.

00:09:09.770 --> 00:09:14.070
Strange, it should be here.

00:09:14.070 --> 00:09:15.490
Mother.

00:09:17.360 --> 00:09:18.820
Mother?

00:09:19.780 --> 00:09:21.490
Naozumi?

00:09:21.490 --> 00:09:31.250
When we first meet I felt that you were my mother.

00:09:31.710 --> 00:09:34.010
Naozumi...

00:09:34.010 --> 00:09:37.680
There is something I would like to show you.

00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:40.260
Here, this is your room!

00:09:40.260 --> 00:09:43.560
You can play on all these things here!

00:09:43.560 --> 00:09:48.230
Like this, anytime you want to play.

00:09:49.650 --> 00:09:52.690
I'm sorry, something got into me.

00:09:53.030 --> 00:09:54.610
Errr...

00:09:55.240 --> 00:10:01.450
Up to this day I lived without knowing anything about my parents.

00:10:01.450 --> 00:10:09.080
It's not something I felt sad or lonely about.

00:10:11.170 --> 00:10:20.010
But here in New York now that I've met you, I'm not so confident anymore.

00:10:20.010 --> 00:10:22.430
I feel a little confused.

00:10:22.430 --> 00:10:27.520
But now I think it's good that I've met you.

00:10:28.060 --> 00:10:37.240
Even if it's just knowing that my mother is alive. I'm happy about that.

00:10:39.360 --> 00:10:48.250
But still, I think I want to live alone.

00:10:48.250 --> 00:10:54.840
Alone, just like before.
That's what I've decided.

00:10:55.960 --> 00:10:59.470
I'm alright.
Please don't worry about me.

00:10:59.470 --> 00:11:02.930
But I want to be worried! Naozumi...

00:11:02.930 --> 00:11:06.310
I want to care about you!

00:11:06.770 --> 00:11:11.400
I've never forgotten you,
not even for a moment!

00:11:20.820 --> 00:11:24.830
I want to stay like this forever...

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:30.160
Goodbye!

00:11:30.160 --> 00:11:32.500
Naozumi! Wait!

00:11:36.090 --> 00:11:39.260
Naozumi! Don't go!

00:11:45.640 --> 00:11:47.060
Naozumi!

00:11:52.230 --> 00:11:53.060
Damn...

00:11:57.980 --> 00:12:03.070
{parte b}

00:12:06.160 --> 00:12:09.040
One, Two, One, Two, Three, Ten!

00:12:09.040 --> 00:12:11.660
Traditional japanese dishes. Tendon is rice and fried fish. Oyakodon is chicken and egg on rice.

00:12:09.040 --> 00:12:11.660
Tendon, yuudon, oyakodon,

00:12:11.960 --> 00:12:14.630
And Babbit likes it, machaudon!

00:12:15.000 --> 00:12:17.670
Tendon, yuudon, oyakodon,

00:12:17.960 --> 00:12:20.630
And Babbit likes it, machaudon!

00:12:21.170 --> 00:12:24.010
That is all for today!
Let's dig in now!

00:12:24.340 --> 00:12:28.390
Welcome Sicil!
Nice to have you in our home!

00:12:28.390 --> 00:12:31.140
Thank you! I'm so happy!

00:12:31.140 --> 00:12:34.980
All right, let's begin this meal right away.

00:12:34.980 --> 00:12:37.060
Bon appetit!

00:12:37.060 --> 00:12:39.860
Mmmm, this is delicious.
You are great, Bernie.

00:12:39.860 --> 00:12:42.780
I'm glad you like it.

00:12:42.780 --> 00:12:44.450
Do you like it, Naozumi?

00:12:44.450 --> 00:12:45.950
Yes, it's delicious.

00:12:45.950 --> 00:12:48.580
That's great. I helped stir it!

00:12:48.580 --> 00:12:51.580
You did? That's wonderful!

00:12:51.580 --> 00:12:55.080
Whee, Naozumi praised me! I'm so happy!

00:12:55.080 --> 00:12:58.670
Hey Sicil, please don't hug me so close!

00:13:00.250 --> 00:13:01.760
Sicil's enjoying herself.

00:13:01.760 --> 00:13:04.970
I can't help it, I'm happy.
Right, Naozumi?

00:13:04.970 --> 00:13:06.180
Crap.

00:13:09.260 --> 00:13:11.390
Ah. Hayama-style.

00:13:11.390 --> 00:13:16.690
This week... everyone.
The party was fun, wasn't it, Sicil-chan?

00:13:22.360 --> 00:13:23.690
Naozumi-kun!

00:13:23.690 --> 00:13:25.780
Ah, Sana-chan.

00:13:25.780 --> 00:13:29.070
I just thought you were playing it.

00:13:29.070 --> 00:13:34.870
Ah, the trumpet? I can't play this well.

00:13:34.870 --> 00:13:38.380
New York's night view is pretty, isn't it?

00:13:38.380 --> 00:13:39.790
Yes.

00:13:42.460 --> 00:13:45.590
I went to meet that person.

00:13:46.130 --> 00:13:48.800
My mother was crying.

00:13:51.100 --> 00:13:54.980
She hugged me, and cried.

00:13:56.690 --> 00:14:03.530
When we met I knew at first sight that she was my mother.

00:14:05.440 --> 00:14:09.030
It was the same with me.
I knew right away.

00:14:09.030 --> 00:14:11.160
Ah, that time.

00:14:14.450 --> 00:14:20.830
But anyway, even though I've met her now, my life will remain the same.

00:14:20.830 --> 00:14:24.960
I think I will live alone by myself
just like before.

00:14:24.960 --> 00:14:28.760
My family is everyone at the Kamura institute.

00:14:29.840 --> 00:14:32.470
So that's what I told her.

00:14:32.470 --> 00:14:33.760
I see.

00:14:33.760 --> 00:14:40.060
Somehow I feel relieved. Thank you for listening to me, Sana-chan.

00:14:40.060 --> 00:14:41.650
Sure.

00:14:43.440 --> 00:14:45.440
So in New York...

00:14:45.440 --> 00:14:46.820
Yes, New York.

00:14:46.940 --> 00:14:49.280
I wonder how Sicil-chan is doing?

00:14:49.280 --> 00:14:53.370
Stop! She got tired after being so enthusiastic, and fell asleep. Please be quiet.

00:14:53.370 --> 00:14:55.410
One, Two, Three!

00:15:57.260 --> 00:15:59.770
I'm worn out!

00:16:04.650 --> 00:16:09.030
Just keeping this up is tiring enough. What an imperfect ending.

00:16:13.450 --> 00:16:15.740
How long do you plan on staying out here?

00:16:15.740 --> 00:16:18.540
Mi-Mi-Mi-Michelle-san!

00:16:18.540 --> 00:16:20.750
I told you I was going to give you a lesson.

00:16:20.750 --> 00:16:22.460
Hurry up, come inside for the training.

00:16:24.330 --> 00:16:27.340
Thank you very much,
thank you very much!

00:16:30.260 --> 00:16:32.970
Sana, Naozumi! Legs higher!

00:16:32.970 --> 00:16:34.130
Yes!

00:16:34.130 --> 00:16:36.260
Reach out further! More, more!

00:16:36.260 --> 00:16:37.970
Yes!

00:16:47.060 --> 00:16:49.270
Hi, Sicil!

00:16:51.150 --> 00:16:52.650
Thank you for waiting!

00:16:52.650 --> 00:16:54.070
Wow, it's huge!

00:16:54.070 --> 00:16:56.870
I will be right back, just wait here for a little while.

00:16:56.870 --> 00:16:57.870
Yes!

00:17:04.670 --> 00:17:05.670
Brad!

00:17:05.670 --> 00:17:06.380
Sicil!

00:17:06.380 --> 00:17:08.670
What's with the scary face?

00:17:08.670 --> 00:17:13.970
I told you I'm not going back!
Not for Papa, Mama, or anyone else.

00:17:13.970 --> 00:17:16.760
I made up my mind to stay here.

00:17:18.680 --> 00:17:20.390
Is it that good?

00:17:20.390 --> 00:17:24.140
Yes, it's so fun to be out with everybody.

00:17:25.350 --> 00:17:29.860
You were always kept at the mansion, so it's natural you're enjoying the outside world.

00:17:29.860 --> 00:17:33.360
No, it's because I can be with Naozumi!

00:17:33.360 --> 00:17:37.490
Everything is so much fun when I am with Naozumi. It makes me so happy!

00:17:37.490 --> 00:17:40.740
When I'm finished here we'll go shopping with Bernie,

00:17:40.740 --> 00:17:45.290
and I'll make delicious dinner for Naozumi! Just perfect, isn't it?

00:17:45.290 --> 00:17:47.670
Sicil, be careful, this is dangerous!

00:17:47.670 --> 00:17:50.790
Really! Anyone would do that for a loved one.

00:17:50.790 --> 00:17:53.800
I'll do the cooking and wait for him to come home! Great, isn't it?

00:17:53.800 --> 00:18:00.350
Sicil! You can't be together with Naozumi forever! He'll return to Japan, eventually.

00:18:00.350 --> 00:18:04.270
I know! But I'll go with him to Japan.

00:18:04.270 --> 00:18:07.440
Do you love him that much?

00:18:07.440 --> 00:18:13.070
Yes, I do! I love him very much!
I can't live without Naozumi anymore!

00:18:14.280 --> 00:18:16.190
Sicil...

00:18:16.530 --> 00:18:18.450
Thank you for waiting, Sicil.

00:18:18.450 --> 00:18:20.740
Sure! Bye, Brad!

00:18:20.740 --> 00:18:22.160
Ah, Sicil!

00:18:22.160 --> 00:18:26.750
Come on, let's hurry! Naozumi will be hungry when he gets back.

00:18:26.750 --> 00:18:28.170
See you later, boss.

00:18:28.170 --> 00:18:32.090
I don't get it. I just don't get it!

00:18:34.960 --> 00:18:37.630
Sicil-chan is making dinner.

00:18:37.630 --> 00:18:43.260
That's the way. The meat will be tender if you cut it up in small pieces like that.

00:18:43.260 --> 00:18:45.470
But I wonder if Naozumi will like it.

00:18:45.470 --> 00:18:49.270
Don't worry. Cooking takes love, and you have plenty of that, right?

00:18:49.270 --> 00:18:51.860
Why doesn't Sicil cook for Babbit with love?

00:18:51.860 --> 00:18:57.150
Oh come on, Bernie! If I keep this up I'll be Naozumi's bride soon.

00:18:57.150 --> 00:19:00.660
Sicil's going to be a bride at 12.

